.SH NAME
lock \- lock a process in primary memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int lock
.I (flag)
.br
\fBint \fIflag\fR;
.SH DESCRIPTION
If the
.I flag
argument is nonzero, the process executing this call is not swapped
except if it is required to grow.
If the argument is zero, the process is
.RB un lock ed.
This call can be executed only by the super-user.
.SH LIMITATIONS
.BR Lock ed
processes interfere with the compaction of primary memory
and can cause deadlock.
This system call is not considered
a permanent part of the system.
.SH ASSEMBLER
.nf
.na
	CONSTANT LOCK	:= 53

	...		!* flag in r0 *!
	clr	r4
	sc	#LOCK
	...		!* return value in r4 *!
	   		!* carry flag set if error *!
.fi
.ad
